{"duration_api_ms":236606,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"df43431f-31a0-49b8-82ab-1cfa11f1a251","total_cost_usd":0.287772,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12702,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":23696,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17506},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12702,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23696,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12702},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":23696,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12702,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.287772,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17506,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 1 of 20 evaluated designs is feasible (C-ee454ee3df8f: 578.9 kW/m2, 432.1 K). 11 of 20 failed geometry. Constraint limits back-calculated from the margins: max_g 12, bondline temperature 450 K. Heatshield mass fraction grows steeply with diameter and is binding by about D 3.3 m. The geometry failures fit a single rule. Taking nose radius as roughly bluntness*D, the fore cone goes negative when bluntness*cos(cone_half_angle) is above about 0.5. Every valid row has B*cos(theta) <= 0.46 and every failed row has >= 0.53. Peak flux scales roughly as D^-1.65 * B^-0.5 * sqrt(sin|gamma|). Bondline temperature falls with lower flux and with steeper entry. max_g rises with steeper entry, about 10.8 g at -3.1 deg and 13.2 g at -4.1 deg, so gamma is capped near -3.6 deg.\",\"evidence\":[\"Geometry-valid rows have B*cos(theta): ee454 0.41, 63010 0.18, fae3 0.22, f84c 0.37, b545 0.35, 4cf8 0.23, 0942 0.31, 23d5 0.46, 9465 0.33. Failed rows: ad22 0.53, 7e34 0.56, 2e54 0.56, 3348 0.52, 2ffd 0.60, b4b6 0.60, 9f9d 0.70, 709f 0.86, 6cb2 0.92, 8a28 1.09, e079 1.08. The threshold sits between 0.46 and 0.52.\",\"Flux scaling: 63010 (B 0.315, D 2.08) has 900 kW/m2 against 579 kW/m2 for ee454 (B 0.674, D 2.23) at nearly the same gamma, which fits flux ~ 1/sqrt(nose radius). Larger D gives much lower flux: f84c (D 3.34) 349 kW/m2 at -5.5 deg, 4cf8 (D 4.05) 302 kW/m2 at -4.1 deg.\",\"g limit: ee454 10.8 g at -3.12 deg, 63010 10.96 g at -3.18 deg, 4cf8 13.16 g at -4.07 deg, fae3 9.24 g at -1.75 deg. About 2.5 g per degree puts the 12 g limit near -3.6 deg.\",\"Bondline temperature: fae3 at -1.75 deg is 470.7 K (infeasible) while 4cf8 at -4.07 deg is 387 K. Shallow entry means a long heat pulse and a hot bondline.\",\"Mass fraction margin: 4cf8 (D 4.05) -0.52, 23d5 (D 4.2) -0.98, 9465 (D 4.49) -0.77, f84c (D 3.34) +0.010, b545 (D 3.19) +0.007. Keep D at or below about 3.2-3.3.\",\"Current hypervolume is 0.092. That equals the feasible point's (1-579/2500)*(1-132/150). The bondline-temperature axis has a lot of headroom to gain.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating falls with nose radius (~Rn^-0.5). Nose radius here is roughly B*D, and larger D also lowers the ballistic coefficient, so flux drops strongly with D. Bondline temperature follows the heat load: lower flux and steeper, shorter entries both cool it. The g limit caps steepness at about -3.6 deg and the mass-fraction limit caps D near 3.2 m. The best region is therefore large D (2.8-3.3 m), large bluntness paired with a large cone angle so that B*cos(theta) stays about 0.42-0.44 (geometry-valid), and gamma about -3.3 to -3.6 deg. The flux, temperature and g scalings come from fitting the 9 valid rows plus general hypersonic-heating knowledge (stagnation-point heating ~ Rn^-0.5).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The geometry rule is fitted from 20 rows. The exact nose-radius definition is not verified, because the reported negative lengths only partly match my formula. The flux exponent on D and the temperature model are extrapolations from few points. Whether max_g depends on D or cone angle is unknown, so the g boundary near -3.6 to -3.8 deg is uncertain. The mass-fraction dependence on cone angle and bluntness is only roughly inferred.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"Large D, high bluntness with steep-ish cone, B*cos(theta)=0.43 for valid geometry, gamma near the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.02,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Core candidate for a big hypervolume jump: low flux and low bondline temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9465c5b873fa\",\"rationale\":\"Shrink D to about 3.0 m to satisfy mass fraction while keeping high B and theta (Bc=0.43).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether a very blunt nose (Rn ~ 3.6 m) gives the lowest flux at feasible D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D with moderate cone angle, B*cos(theta)=0.43.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.86,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":298000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates cone-angle effect from the high-B designs at similar D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ee454ee3df8f\",\"rationale\":\"Grow D of the only feasible design and keep its cone angle region, with slightly steeper entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.67,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":50.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":396000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-risk local improvement on the known feasible design; measures D sensitivity.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9465c5b873fa\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D (2.6 m) with maximum bluntness at theta 70; probes lower-mass corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":354000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the trade-off front at smaller D and tests g at -3.6 deg with high theta.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.0, B 1.0, theta 64, gamma a bit shallower than the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safer g margin variant of the core candidate.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ee454ee3df8f\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate D 2.5 with B 0.8 and theta 57 at gamma -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.5,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":57.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":445000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":419,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolates near the known feasible design and extends the front toward smaller size.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b545729400dd\",\"rationale\":\"Lower cone angle 45 deg with B 0.62 (Bc=0.44); tests cone-angle effect on flux, mass and g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.62,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":45.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":368000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether a lower cone angle costs mass fraction near D 3.1.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to -3.7 to probe the g limit at D 3.2 with theta 66.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the max_g boundary; a pass would lower bondline temperature further.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9465c5b873fa\",\"rationale\":\"Deliberately steep gamma -3.8 at large D and bluntness to map where g fails.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":388,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Bracket for the g constraint and D dependence of g; if feasible it dominates.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.3 close to the mass-fraction limit with B 0.95, theta 63.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.95,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":63.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":266000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the mass-fraction boundary; f84c at D 3.34 had margin only +0.010.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ee454ee3df8f\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-range D 2.8, B 0.9, theta 62 for coverage.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":358000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the mid-front with a safe design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9465c5b873fa\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.7, B 1.1, theta 67.5 at gamma -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.7,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":340000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a mid-D blunt design to check the D^-1.65 flux scaling.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.0, B 1.05, theta 66, gamma -3.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":306000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Second g probe at -3.6 deg with smaller D than the -3.7 case.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9465c5b873fa\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.8, max bluntness at theta 70, gamma -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":304000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the D effect versus the -3.6 deg, D 2.6 m variant.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4cf8bee56534\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate cone angle 58 with B 0.8 at D 3.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":58.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":324000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the theta dimension between 45 and 65 deg at similar D and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-23d51d53a5ac\",\"rationale\":\"Low cone angle 40 deg with B 0.55 at D 2.9; tests mass and geometry at low theta.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.55,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":40.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":420000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the geometry rule holds at low theta and how mass fraction responds.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ee454ee3df8f\",\"rationale\":\"Grow D to 3.0 at nearly the same cone angle, B 0.7 (Bc=0.42).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":53.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":368000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct D-sensitivity step from the feasible design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63010bee087f\",\"rationale\":\"Raise B from 0.315 to 0.6 with theta 47 to fix the hot bondline while keeping valid geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":47.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":415000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Converts a near-feasible design into a feasible one and adds moderate-theta coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9465c5b873fa\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.1, B 1.1, theta 67, gamma -3.45.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Another near-optimum candidate varying B and theta slightly, to pick the best cell of the local grid.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":188701,"type":"result","duration_ms":236766,"uuid":"455773a9-87c8-40ca-a040-3460333b1149","ttft_stream_ms":1605,"time_to_request_ms":160,"first_content_frame_ms":1605,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
